                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "27d5d724-a2d7-3c10-8724-370212e110ee",
                        "entry_id": "be298fb4-367a-3c2e-b842-2d82cbcb2843",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To disseminate, promulgate, or spread news, a rumour, etc."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "archaic",
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "04f2ec32-8379-4ca6-9ad3-971a95ca99f2",
                                "sense_id": "27d5d724-a2d7-3c10-8724-370212e110ee",
                                "text": "And if it be to be beleued, as bruted is by fame. / A day did paſſe without the Sunne."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "54443e95-ab97-4f76-a7f8-095fad202300",
                                "sense_id": "27d5d724-a2d7-3c10-8724-370212e110ee",
                                "text": "Generally, Whether there be [...] any that stubbornly refuse to conform themselves to unity and good religion: any that bruiteth abroad rumours of the alteration of the same, or otherwise that disturbeth good orders, and the quietnes of Christs Church and Christian congregation."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4a89c4b7-b8cd-40c0-b2f0-e1c2485db056",
                                "sense_id": "27d5d724-a2d7-3c10-8724-370212e110ee",
                                "text": "There haue bin diuers and variable reportes with some slaunderous and shamefull speeches bruited abroade by many that returned from thence."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0af47a0d-4857-4c44-8d30-41761cd516e6",
                                "sense_id": "27d5d724-a2d7-3c10-8724-370212e110ee",
                                "text": "And the Kings rowſe the heauen shall brute againe, / Reſpeaking earthly thunder; [...]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "801c82ed-a2be-45bb-8215-343ac8bcb49b",
                                "sense_id": "27d5d724-a2d7-3c10-8724-370212e110ee",
                                "text": "Even his amours he bruits forth to the public, to the delight of every pot-boy."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d1eb19b0-455c-405b-8e46-ee4904e00f2c",
                                "sense_id": "27d5d724-a2d7-3c10-8724-370212e110ee",
                                "text": "As he took John Willet's view of the matter in regard to the propriety of not bruiting the tale abroad, unless the spirit should appear to him again, in which case it would be necessary to take immediate counsel with the clergyman, it was solemnly resolved that it should be hushed up and kept quiet."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "27f25f48-39f5-4e71-b0c7-029a9a8b58ee",
                                "sense_id": "27d5d724-a2d7-3c10-8724-370212e110ee",
                                "text": "In course of time Ariston died; and Demaratus received the kingdom: but it was fated, as it seems, that these words, when bruited abroad, should strip him of his sovereignty."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "fd99a947-d51f-4a65-bad1-4e02fabdce41",
                                "sense_id": "27d5d724-a2d7-3c10-8724-370212e110ee",
                                "text": "What need to bruit our pleasant quarrel abroad? You will like the weapons, sir, and you shall have your own choice from the pair … You are a fine fencer, I feel sure …"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e09efed8-3ce0-42cc-bde5-029df4dcce8b",
                                "sense_id": "27d5d724-a2d7-3c10-8724-370212e110ee",
                                "text": "Thou art not ware, but thou art tossed on the tongues of all the city, casting away all shame, thou bruitest abroad thy deeds."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4ff888b1-6c45-4464-ba1d-d77aa864e440",
                                "sense_id": "27d5d724-a2d7-3c10-8724-370212e110ee",
                                "text": "TV news shows had been bruiting the Boulder case, too; as a result, the atmosphere in the press section that night was knife-keen."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "fbc7ff66-3d90-45cd-9682-507bc618182c",
                                "sense_id": "27d5d724-a2d7-3c10-8724-370212e110ee",
                                "text": "Paranoid. Now he knew what it meant, this word that was bandied and bruited so easily, and he sensed the connections being made around him, [...]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2259a965-99ea-4c67-b721-96371b858cc1",
                                "sense_id": "27d5d724-a2d7-3c10-8724-370212e110ee",
                                "text": "[I]t's bruited that the tunnel would cost \"10 to 20 million yuan ($2.95 million) more than the current high speed railway for each kilometer.\" Pony up, taxpayers!"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c179c6a5-b20d-452e-a0d9-f18e3d882f5d",
                                "sense_id": "27d5d724-a2d7-3c10-8724-370212e110ee",
                                "text": "Bruiting about this notion of a \"monarchical project,\" the Englishman persuaded himself that [Simón] Bolívar himself aspired to such a model."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "48c96b23-3f82-423f-86a9-e08dccc7d4d4",
                        "source_entry_id": "be298fb4-367a-3c2e-b842-2d82cbcb2843",
                        "source_sense_id": "27d5d724-a2d7-3c10-8724-370212e110ee",
                        "source_sense_description": "to disseminate, promulgate, or spread news, a rumour, etc.",
                        "target_lang_word": "ébruiter",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "ébruiter",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "88ab39ec-486c-3405-bd5e-b73747025a97",
                                        "entry_id": "e9978ed6-cbe3-3be4-8425-3dffd6090b70",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Divulguer, rendre public."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2a6f0ef9-e3a2-4ab9-adbb-226df0f784e9",
                                                "sense_id": "88ab39ec-486c-3405-bd5e-b73747025a97",
                                                "text": "Elle nous a suppliés de ne point ébruiter notre rencontre, mais elle ne s'est point opposée, au contraire, à ce que nous venions passer tout le temps qu’il nous plairait dans le jardin de sa maison."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "762a06bd-15f6-414b-a213-f60178b59d25",
                                                "sense_id": "88ab39ec-486c-3405-bd5e-b73747025a97",
                                                "text": "La dame brûlait du désir d’ébruiter une nouvelle dont elle venait d’avoir la primeur."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "word_linkages": []
            }
        ],
